Rate-limit the "Cache mode %x not implemented" warning.

PR SCOPE: OUT. Log noise only, no behaviour change.

Applies to a clean tree; independent of the other patches.

Games barely touch the EE cache instruction, so Cache.cpp logs every unhandled
mode. A real OS does cache maintenance on every context switch and for DMA
coherency: one BlackRhino boot emitted 251,370 of these -- 95% of the entire
log, which came to 268,116 lines. With this and the branch-delay limit, the same
boot logs 14,537.

Rate-limited to 50 rather than silenced, so the first occurrences still report
which modes are missing.

--- a/pcsx2/Cache.cpp
+++ b/pcsx2/Cache.cpp
@@ -501,8 +501,14 @@
 					}
 
 					default:
-						DevCon.Warning("Cache mode %x not implemented", _Rt_);
+					{
+						// Rate-limited: rare for games, constant under a real
+						// OS doing cache maintenance.
+						static int s_cacheSpamStop = 0;
+						if (s_cacheSpamStop++ < 50)
+							DevCon.Warning("Cache mode %x not implemented (%d)", _Rt_, s_cacheSpamStop);
 						break;
+					}
 				}
 			}
 		} // end namespace OpcodeImpl
